],"cap":"Revisão integrada — ciência"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Biografias científicas combinam **orações relativas**, **crítica ao passado** e **verbos de relato**."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"Franklin, ___ was born in London, was a chemist. (who)","a":"who","why":"pessoa."},{"s":"Photo 51, ___ was taken in 1952, showed a helix. (which)","a":"which","why":"coisa."},{"s":"Her data should have been ___ . (credit, part.)","a":"credited","why":"passiva."},{"s":"She preferred facts ___ fame. (to)","a":"to","why":"prefer A to B."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["X-ray diffraction","difração de raios X"],["DNA helix","hélice de DNA"],["crystal image","imagem de cristal"],["Photo 51","Fotografia 51"],["King’s College lab","laboratório do King’s College"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["Rosalind","Franklin","Who","was"],"ans":"Who was Rosalind Franklin","pt":"Quem foi Rosalind Franklin?"},{"words":["happened","What","should","have"],"ans":"What should have happened","pt":"O que deveria ter acontecido?"}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"X-ray diffraction","pos":"word","pt":"difração de raios X","ex":"X-ray diffraction.","expt":"Difração de raios X."},{"w":"DNA helix","pos":"word","pt":"hélice de DNA","ex":"DNA helix.","expt":"Hélice de DNA."},{"w":"crystal image","pos":"word","pt":"imagem de cristal","ex":"Crystal image.","expt":"Imagem de cristal."},{"w":"Photo 51","pos":"word","pt":"Fotografia 51","ex":"Photo 51.","expt":"Fotografia 51."},{"w":"King’s College lab","pos":"word","pt":"laboratório do King’s College","ex":"King’s College lab.","expt":"Laboratório do King’s College."},{"w":"molecular structure","pos":"word","pt":"estrutura molecular","ex":"Molecular structure.","expt":"Estrutura molecular."},{"w":"double-h