ova luz.","**Who was Rosalind Franklin?** — Quem foi Rosalind Franklin?","**What should have happened?** — O que deveria ter acontecido?","**A chemist whose X-ray images of DNA were crucial.** — Uma química cujas imagens de raios X do DNA foram cruciais."]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"credit","pt":"dar crédito a","forms":[["I / you / we / they credit","Always credit your sources."],["he / she / it credits","Sempre credite suas fontes."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Class","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Class","lines":[["Ana","Who was Rosalind Franklin?","Quem foi Rosalind Franklin?"],["Leo","A chemist whose X-ray images of DNA were crucial.","Uma química cujas imagens de raios X do DNA foram cruciais."],["Ana","What should have happened?","O que deveria ter acontecido?"],["Leo","Her data should have been credited more openly.","Seus dados deveriam ter sido creditados com mais transparência."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Acento para enfatizar informação","items":[{"label":"Acento para enfatizar informação","note":"A palavra nova ou importante recebe o acento mais forte: I want the RED one, not the blue one.","words":["I want the RED one.","She said TUESDAY.","Not TWO, THREE.","He BOUGHT it."]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Describe a person with who.","pt":"Descreva.","model":"She was a chemist who loved facts."},{"q":"Use whose.","pt":"Use.","model":"She was a scientist whose work mattered."},{"q":"Use should have been.","pt":"Use.","model":"Her work should have been recognised."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a 6-sentence biography of a scientist you admire.","model":"Rosalind Franklin, who was born in London in 1920, was a chemist. Her Photo 51, which was taken in 1952, showed a helix pattern. Colleagues admitted later that her data should have been credited more openly. She died at 37. She preferred facts to fame. Today she is remembered with respect.","checklist":["Usei **, who**","Usei **, which**","Usei **should have been**"],"words":"6 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “X-ray diffraction” mean?","opts":["hélice de DNA","difração de raios X","Fotografia 51"],"ans":1,"why":"**X-ray diffraction** = difração de raios X."},{"q":"What does “DNA helix” mean?","opts":["imagem de cristal","laboratório do King’s College","hélice de DNA"],"ans":2,"why":"**DNA helix** = hélice de DNA."},{"q":"What does “crystal image” mean?","opts":["imagem de cristal","Fotografia 51","estrutura molecular"],"ans":0,"why":"**crystal image** = imagem de cristal."},{"q":"What does “Photo 51” mean?","opts":["laboratório do King’s College","Fotografia 51","modelo de dupla hélice"],"ans":1,"why":"**Photo 51** = Fotografia 51."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}